        "title": "refactor(config): remove dead session runtime exports",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe session runtime type contract retained five unused maintenance/store exports that duplicated the private types owned by the session store implementation. They enlarged the internal runtime surface and required permanent dead-export baseline exemptions despite having no callers.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nRemove the unused declarations and their now-unused import, then delete the matching dead-export baseline entries. The three runtime types still consumed by plugin channel bindings remain unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior changes. Maintainers get a smaller session runtime contract with one fewer duplicate representation of store maintenance options.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxd9qm82f898nzcr6cv2sre8`, Actions run `29235835458`:\n  - `corepack pnpm deadcode:exports` passed; the Knip unused-export baseline matched 3,535 entries.\n  - touched-path `pnpm check:changed` passed for `scripts/deadcode-exports.baseline.mjs` and `src/config/sessions/runtime-types.ts`.\n- `gpt-5.6-sol` autoreview at medium reasoning: clean, confidence `0.98`.\n- `oxfmt --check` and `git diff --check` passed.\n",
